// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`verifier handoff template snapshots > 'duo' 'planner' → 'verifier' renders the complete contract 1`] = `
"> ⚠️ **Template notice — not part of the message. Do not copy this notice into your handoff.**
> Recipient visibility: the \`verifier\` agent receives only the text inside your \`handoff --next-role="verifier"\` command. It cannot see anything you write in this agent session, or tool output. Put your complete deliverable in the handoff message.

Handoff template \`planner\` → \`verifier\` (copy only the body sections below; do not copy this line, the notice, or the instructions after the body):

Instructions (not part of the message): The verifier judges, from chatroom logs only, whether the user's last message was achieved. It runs no test the user did not ask for, and never builds, lints, or edits; list any user-requested tests under Requested test runs. Treat the claimed outcome as a claim, not as evidence: the verifier does not trust it and checks every requirement against the logs themselves. List every message id that carries the claimed work under Log message ids, so the verifier can read those messages from the logs. Request this review whenever the task produced a deliverable (code, docs, review, research, or asset), in any conversation mode; skip it only for pure conversation with no deliverable. Finish every other user-required step first (for example a push, or a PR the user asked for), and record its command and result in a message listed under Log message ids. A step that can only follow the verdict, such as backlog \`chatroom backlog mark-for-review\` for an attached backlog item, goes under Known gaps as \`pending after verdict: <step>\`; the verifier does not count it as unmet or unverified.

Evidence to record for each deliverable type you name, in a message before you send this request, and list that message under Log message ids:
- \`code\`: commit hashes; pushed and clean-tree evidence (a push result, or a clean \`git status\`, quoted in a message); the PR URL when a PR was raised; typecheck, lint, and test results quoted in a message
- \`docs\`: the changed documentation file paths; commit and push evidence when the docs are tracked in the repository; the PR URL when a PR was raised
- \`review\`: the review report message, naming the reviewed target (commit range, PR, or file list) and each finding
- \`research\`: the findings message that answers each research question, with its sources (URLs, file paths, or message ids)
- \`asset\`: the generated asset output paths; the game-asset-designer checklist results with their evidence labels; the asset-in-rig render when the brief required one

The verdict returns to \`planner\`.

## Round
<1 or 2; for 2, cite the round-1 verdict message id>

## Mode
<chat | code>

## Deliverable type
<code | docs | review | research | asset; comma-separated when the work produced more than one>

## User message id
<id of the user's last message: the origin message id of the user task, or from \`chatroom messages anchor\`>

## Log message ids
<one per line as \`<message id> — <sender role> — <what it shows>\`: every message that carries the claimed work, in order: builder and specialist handoff reports, the reviewer report, and the evidence messages for each deliverable type; or exactly \`None beyond the user message.\`>

## Requested test runs
<the test commands the user explicitly asked for, one per line, or exactly \`None requested.\`>

## Claimed outcome
<requirement-by-requirement what you believe is complete>

## Evidence pointers
<the evidence for each deliverable type named above, as quoted in the messages listed under Log message ids>

## Known gaps
<anything incomplete, including each \`pending after verdict: <step>\` line, or exactly \`None.\`>

Instructions after the body (not part of the message): run the normal handoff command to \`planner\` with the complete body above, then stop.

\`\`\`bash
chatroom handoff --chatroom-id="<chatroom-id>" --role="planner" --next-role="verifier" << 'CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your message here]
CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END
\`\`\`

### Grounding reference
Add this section to your message. Replace the placeholder with the id of the newest grounding message you published for this request, or write \`None.\`.

\`\`\`markdown
## Grounding
Grounding ID: <groundingId>, or \`None.\`
Read it: \`chatroom grounding read --chatroom-id="<chatroom-id>" --role="verifier" --grounding-id="<groundingId>"\`
It records preliminary, factual observations from an earlier pass. Treat it as a starting point, not as verified truth: re-check every file, symbol and flow you rely on against the repository, and prefer the code where they differ.
\`\`\`"
`;

exports[`verifier handoff template snapshots > 'duo' 'verifier' → 'planner' renders the complete contract 1`] = `
"> ⚠️ **Template notice — not part of the message. Do not copy this notice into your handoff.**
> Recipient visibility: the \`planner\` agent receives only the text inside your \`handoff --next-role="planner"\` command. It cannot see anything you write in this agent session, or tool output. Put your complete deliverable in the handoff message.

Handoff template \`verifier\` → \`planner\` (copy only the body sections below; do not copy this line, the notice, or the instructions after the body):

Instructions (not part of the message): Return one advisory verdict for the authoritative request. This review is non-binding: it uses chatroom logs, plus the requested test runs listed in the request, if any, deciding every requirement from the evidence those logs and runs actually contain. It also checks the work against the user's expectations (\`## User Expectations\`) under the same logs-only, claim-is-not-evidence rule. It runs no test the user did not ask for, and never builds, lints, or edits. Never accept the claimed outcome as proof. Use the exact sections below, in this order.

## Verdict
<exactly one of ACHIEVED, NOT_ACHIEVED, INCONCLUSIVE as the value; ACHIEVED only if every requirement and user expectation is met; NOT_ACHIEVED if any requirement or user expectation is unmet (logs show it was not done, or contradict it); INCONCLUSIVE if none is unmet but any is unverified (logs are silent)>

## Objective
<user message id, any prior user messages used, objective in 1-2 sentences>

## Requirements
<numbered \`R1 — <requirement> — met | unmet | unverified — <evidence ref>\`>

## User Expectations
<numbered \`U1 — <expectation from the user's handoff template that applies to the deliverable type(s) named in the request> — met | unmet | unverified — <evidence ref>\`; exactly \`None applicable.\` in chat mode or when no expectation applies>

## Evidence
<bullets: \`<message id or handoff> — "<short quote>" — supports R#\`; for a requested test run, \`<command> — exit <result> — supports R#\`>

## Missing or unmet
<per unmet or unverified requirement or user expectation: what is missing and what evidence would resolve it; exactly \`None.\` if ACHIEVED>

## Scope and limits
<state the test runs the verifier executed (command and exit result), or "No tests were run; none were requested."; the log range read (first and last message id, and the message count); whether the download was truncated; which Log message ids were found in that range and which were not; each \`pending after verdict\` step the request listed that you accepted under step 4a, named as not checked>

Instructions after the body (not part of the message): run the normal handoff command to \`planner\` with the complete body above, then stop.

\`\`\`bash
chatroom handoff --chatroom-id="<chatroom-id>" --role="verifier" --next-role="planner" << 'CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END'
---MESSAGE---
[Your message here]
CHATROOM_HANDOFF_END
\`\`\`"
`;

